5,000 to 15,000 tokens for each of 2 or 3 shops, and the judgement. Energy: 3 to 15 ordinary queries."}},"scenarios":[{"perDay":1000,"tokensPerDay":[3800000,13000000,34500000],"kwhPerDay":[0.4,1.6,4.4],"mwhPerYear":[0.2,0.6,1.6]},{"perDay":100000,"tokensPerDay":[380000000,1300000000,3450000000],"kwhPerDay":[44,160,437],"mwhPerYear":[16.1,58.4,159.5]},{"perDay":10000000,"tokensPerDay":[38000000000,130000000000,345000000000],"kwhPerDay":[4400,16000,43700],"mwhPerYear":[1606,5840,15950.5]},{"perDay":1000000000,"tokensPerDay":[3800000000000,13000000000000,34500000000000],"kwhPerDay":[440000,1600000,4370000],"mwhPerYear":[160600,584000,1595050]}],"mix":{"path":0.5,"plan":0.3,"market":0.2},"sources":[{"what":"Energy of one query to a frontier model: median 0.31 Wh (0.16–0.60); a long reasoning query (test-time scaling, about 5,000 output tokens) 3.91 Wh (2.15–7.05)","by":"Oviedo et al., Joule (2026), doi 10.1016/j.joule.2026.102430","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.20241"},{"what":"Median Gemini text prompt: 0.24 Wh","by":"Google (August 2025)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.15734"},{"what":"Tokens of one agent task: about 26,000 input and 4,700 output at the easiest GAIA level, 121,000 and 9,800 at the hardest","by":"Memento, arXiv 2508.16153","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.16153"},{"what":"Agents use about 4 times the tokens of a chat, systems of several agents about 15 times","by":"Anthropic engineering (June 2025)","url":"https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/multi-agent-research-system"},{"what":"Data centres used about 415 TWh in 2024, about 1.5 % of the world's electricity, heading for about 945 TWh by 2030","by":"IEA, Energy and AI (2025)","url":"https://www.iea.org/reports/energy-and-ai"},{"what":"Data centres used about 485 TWh in 2025, heading for about 950 TWh in 2030","by":"IEA, Key questions on energy and AI (2026)","url":"https://iea.org/reports/key-questions-on-energy-and-ai/executive-summary"}],"notCounted":["the energy of the sea itself (one small server; a lookup is milliseconds of one processor, far below one model query)","Markdown in watt-hours: its tokens are counted as measured, their energy is left out","the time agents and people save, and the fake shops not paid"],"ratio":{"html":3.22,"md":3.58,"text":4.32,"unit":"characters per token (JavaScript string length)","bytes":{"html":3.23,"md":3.59,"text":4.34,"unit":"UTF-8 bytes per token"},"assumption":false,"tokenizer":"o200k_base","date":"2026-11-24","pages":33,"run":"https://mare.test/proof/bench-2026-11-24.json","proof":"https://mare.test/proof","basis":"measured, not assumed: on the 33 pages of the proof of function (2026-11-24, tokenizer o200k_base) one token held 3.22 characters of raw HTML (3.23 UTF-8 bytes), 3.58 of the sea's Markdown (3.59) and 4.32 of plain text (4.34). Each count becomes tokens with the ratio of its form and of the unit it was counted in: UTF-8 bytes for pages of the sea, characters for pages read through the reader and for counts from before 3.33.0","source":{"what":"Characters and UTF-8 bytes per token for raw HTML, plain text and the sea's Markdown, counted with the o200k_base tokenizer on the 33 pages of a published task set","by":"Mare Liberum, proof of function","url":"https://mareliberum.dev/proof"},"fallback":{"html":4,"md":4,"note":"used only when no measured run is present"}},"price":{"asOf":"2026-11-24","unit":"USD per million input tokens","low":0.1,"mid":2,"high":8,"lowIs":"a small model: Claude Haiku 5.5 (prompts up to 100,000 tokens) and Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite are $0.10","midIs":"the workhorse model of each of the three: Claude Sonnet 5.5, gpt-6.2-sol and Gemini 3.1 Pro (prompts up to 200k tokens) are $2","highIs":"the top model: Claude Fable 5.2 and gpt-6.2-astra are $8","label":"list price for uncached input tokens, modelled","sources":[{"what":"Claude Haiku 5.5 $0.10, Claude Sonnet 5.5 $2 and Claude Fable 5.2 $8 per million base input tokens","by":"Anthropic, Claude API pricing","url":"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing"},{"what":"gpt-6.2-sol $2 and gpt-6.2-astra $8 per million input tokens, standard tier","by":"OpenAI API pricing","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing"},{"what":"Gemini 3.1 Pro $2 (prompts up to 200k tokens) and Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite $0.10 per million input tokens, paid tier","by":"Google, Gemini Developer API pricing","url":"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing"}]},"read":"A reuse counts once a day per caller network and task when an answer handed an agent a part someone already solved: a confirmed pathway (path), a ready plan (plan), verified offers (market); what it spares is modelled from the ranges in perReuse (low, mid, high). Markdown is measured: md counts pages of the sea asked for as Markdown, mdAgent pages of the sea sent as Markdown to an assistant reading for a person (md-agent), reads pages of other sites through the reader, each with what it spared against the page as HTML (UTF-8 bytes for pages of the sea, characters for pages through the reader); counts become tokens by one rule (ratio: HTML 3.23 bytes or 3.22 characters a token, Markdown 3.59 bytes or 3.58 characters, measured with o200k_base on the proof of function (https://mare.test/proof)). usd prices the tokens at list prices for uncached input tokens (price): low, mid (the headline) and high. A Markdown answer counts once a day per network and page; one network adds at most 500 Markdown answers and 500 reuses a day. measured is against raw HTML, an upper bound; vsText is the same answers against plain text (pages of the sea), the lower view. The sea's own calls and crawlers are never counted; the house agent (Angel) is counted apart (house)."}}
